title: $:/plugins/cdr/markdown-more/syntax

!! Checklist

```markdown
- [ ] Task 1
- [x] Task 2
```

This plugin provides simple interactive checklists. Clicking on the checkboxes will alter the underlying Markdown text.
To minimize unintended changes, transcluded checklists will be read-only. Care must also be taken when
mixing <$text text="WikiText"/> and the markdown text. For example, if you enter the following:

```
<$list filter="apple bat candle" variable="item">

- [ ] <<item>>

</$list>
```

All of the rendered checkboxes in the example above will be linked to a single toggle state. Clicking on any one of them
will cause all of boxes to be updated.

!! Example Block

Begin an indented example block with `->` followed by a space. You can provide an additional comment section;
anything following the `//` symbol will be treated as comments.

```
Here is an example:

-> Bon Appétit!  // Enjoy your meal!
```

Rendered output:

<div class="markdown" style="border: 1px solid gray;border-radius:5px;padding:2px 5px;">
<p>Here is an example:
</p>
<div class="md-example-container">
<span class="md-example-text">Bon Appétit!</span>
<span class="md-example-comment">Enjoy your meal!</span>
</div>
</div>

!! Admonitions

Create special content blocks with the admonition syntax:

```markdown
::::note Optional title can be specified after the category name
Information the user should notice.

:::summary
Admonition blocks can be nested.
:::

::::
```

You can create collapsible containers by appending `+` (to initially expand) or `-` after the category name.

```
:::note+
Collapsible content
:::
```

Or, to hide the title bar completely, set the custom title message to  `''`.

```
:::note ''
No title bar
:::
```

Available categories are:

* note, info, todo
* important
* tip, success, question
* warning, caution
* fail, danger, error, bug
* example, snippet, abstract, summary
* quote, cite
* see-also

<div class="markdown">
<div class="admonition" data-admonition="note"><div class="admonition-title">NOTE</div></div>
<div class="admonition" data-admonition="info"><div class="admonition-title">INFO</div></div>
