!!! Column Groups

You can define column groups by specifying either pseudo-row type `g` or type `w`. Note that both types are added
by this extension and work only in Markdown tiddlers. These two types are mutually exclusive: `g` defines
column group classes while `w` defines column group widths. A table can contain at most one column group definition
row. Subsequent definition rows will be ignored.

Example 1:

```
|foo|<|bar baz|g
```

The definition above assigns CSS class "foo" to columns 1 and 2 and classes "bar" and "baz" to column 3.

Example 2:

```
||100px|<|w
```

The definition above sets the width of columns 2 and 3 to 100px each.